# The adapter spawns `dsh --profile sdk` as a local harness subprocess and the
# harness reaches the DeepSeek API with this key.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# dsh treats every DSH_* name as LAUNCH-ONLY: the harness child runs with this
# folder as its cwd, so the dsh CLI boot layer reads THIS file too — and aborts
# on any DSH_* (or XDG_*/DYLD_*/...) assignment here. Keep this file free of
# DSH_* keys. To override launch settings, export them in the shell before
# `npm run dev` (e.g. `export DSH_HOME=~/.dsh DSH_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash`).
# Defaults when nothing is set: profile `sdk`, home `~/.dsh`, provider
# `deepseek-official`, model `deepseek-v4-flash`, agent workspace = this folder,
# transcript mirror under the service tmp dir. DSH_TRANSCRIPT_DIR (mirror) and
# DSH_DEFAULT_SESSION (which conversation to resume) are DSH_* too — export
# them if you want them.
